# Citation metadata — GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository".
#
# The abstract deliberately carries the scope statement. Someone who encounters
# this work only as a citation, with no access to the site, still learns that it
# is a design study and that its figures are modelled rather than measured.
# Keep that in any edit; it is the same guardrail the pages carry.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PulseMask: a photo-fitted respirator-form wearable-art design study"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Zach
    family-names: Auerbach
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-3046-9104"
    affiliation: "Aurelius Dynamic"
    email: build@aureliusdynamic.com

repository-code: "https://github.com/ZachBach/helixPulse"
url: "https://github.com/ZachBach/helixPulse"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based parametric generator that produces printable, watertight
  respirator-form geometry from a single portrait photograph and an
  interpupillary distance, published as a wearable-art design study. The
  geometry engine is dependency-free and runs identically in a browser and
  headless in Node, emitting 30 named closed meshes with STL, OBJ and GLB
  export. Rendering uses WebGPU with TSL node materials. Accompanying material
  documents the photogrammetric fit pipeline, an enclosed UV-C reactor concept
  and a piezoelectric transducer array.

  Scope, stated as part of the record: this is NOT a respirator, NOT personal
  protective equipment and NOT a medical device. It is untested to NIOSH
  42 CFR 84, EN 136, EN 143 and ISO 16900, has no regulatory clearance, and
  provides no respiratory protection of any kind. All germicidal,
  log-reduction and capsid-disruption figures are MODELLED, NEVER MEASURED,
  including the reported ultraviolet dose of 0.22 mJ/cm2, which is
  approximately 7 percent of the 3.0 mJ/cm2 target for two-log inactivation
  and is published unrounded as a negative result. Single-image capture cannot
  recover metric depth, so the fit is inferred, not validated.

keywords:
  - wearable art
  - design study
  - parametric geometry
  - photogrammetry
  - 3D printing
  - WebGPU
  - TSL
  - three.js
  - generative design

license: LicenseRef-Proprietary
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
